# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A report is worked out again when the book has changed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description A report tab holds the figures it was worked out with. It is worked
\ out again when it is shown and the book has changed since it was
\ last worked out, and at no other time.
Details Every figure in a report is a total of transactions and nothing is
\ stored, which is the rule in Reports and is what makes a report and a
\ register agree. It also means a report is right the moment it is
\ worked out and wrong the moment a transaction moves, so something has
\ to say when to work it out again. Two answers are wrong. Never, and
\ the page shows last week's totals. Always, and a category report over
\ twenty years is totalled again because somebody clicked a tab -- a
\ redraw happens when a tab is clicked, when an account is selected,
\ when a column is resized, and a report that redoes its work on each of
\ those is the slowest thing in the program by a wide margin.
\
\ So it is the book that decides, not the event: a report is worked out
\ again when the book is not the book it was totalled from. Which change
\ it was does not come into it. A transaction entered outside the
\ report's period still counts as a change, because working out which
\ changes could not possibly have mattered would be a second statement
\ of what a report totals -- in a second place, wrong the first time a
\ period moved.
\
\ And not until it is shown. A report tab nobody is looking at has no
\ figure on screen to be wrong, so the work waits for the click that
\ brings it forward. Each tab remembers the book it was worked out from
\ on its own: two report tabs with one flag between them would leave the
\ second showing stale totals, which is the shape of this bug wherever
\ it has been written before.
\
\ A register is not in any of this. It is read from the book every
\ redraw and always was; it costs a sort of one account's lines, not a
\ walk of the whole book.

Attributes ReportWork
Description How many times the report on one tab has been worked out, counting
\ from when the tab was opened. Register tabs are not listed.
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Position  | Integer | 1       |
| Times     | Integer | 1       |

