# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Showing the transaction an import row was decided against
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description A duplicate is a claim about a transaction that is already in the
\ book, and the claim is worth looking at before it is believed. The
\ review shows the row the file sent; this shows what the import
\ decided the row already was, so that the two can be read side by
\ side and the tick changed if the decision was wrong.

Attributes ImportReviewSelect
Description The line of the import review that is selected, counting from one
\ in the order the review is showing.
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Line      | Integer | 1       |

Attributes ImportReviewClaim
Description What the import decided a review line already was. A line can
\ claim more than one transaction -- a Possible claims every
\ transaction it could be -- so this is a row per claim rather than a
\ field on the row. Line is the review line; Ref is the transaction
\ already in the book.
| Attribute | Type           | Default |
| Line      | Integer        | 0       |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |         |

Attributes DuplicateTransactionDialog
Description What came up. Heading is shown above the transactions because one
\ transaction and three of them mean different things, and the
\ difference is the whole reason the dialog is worth opening.
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Shown     | Boolean | false   |
| Count     | Integer | 0       |
| Heading   | Text    | none    |

Attributes DuplicateTransactionRow
Description One transaction the import claimed, read off the book rather than
\ off the file: this is what is already there.
| Attribute | Type           | Default    |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |            |
| Date      | Date           | 2026-01-01 |
| Payee     | PayeeName      | none       |
| Account   | AccountPath    | none       |
| Category  | AccountPath    | none       |
| Amount    | Money          | 0.00       |
| CheckNo   | CheckNumber    | none       |
| Cleared   | ClearedStatus  | Uncleared  |

Attributes DuplicateMenuRule
| Attribute   | Type              | Default |
| Disposition | ImportDisposition | New     |
| Item        | Text              | none    |
| Enabled     | Boolean           | true    |

BusinessRule What the menu on an import row offers
Description The item reads as the disposition does. A duplicate names one
\ transaction, a possible names several, and a completion names the
\ payment whose other half was waiting -- calling that last one a
\ duplicate would be wrong, because nothing is being refused.
Details A New row claims nothing, so there is nothing to show. The item is
\ still on the menu, disabled, rather than absent: a menu that
\ changes shape from line to line is harder to learn than one item
\ that is sometimes grey.
Examples: DuplicateMenuRule
| Disposition | Item                               | Enabled |
| New         | Show~duplicate~transaction...      | false   |
| Duplicate   | Show~duplicate~transaction...      | true    |
| Possible    | Show~possible~duplicates...        | true    |
| Completed   | Show~the~payment~this~completes... | true    |

