| Accepted   | 2     |
| Committed  | false |
# Both tabs' own content is unaffected by which one is in front; the import's
# rows are still exactly what they were, just not what is showing right now.

Attributes BottomPanelTabSelect
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Tab       | Integer | 0       |

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Find
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description Find looks across transactions for ones matching what was typed,
\ and shows the matches in a tab of the bottom panel, beside the
\ register, the same as an import. There is one Find dialog, so
\ performing a find again replaces that tab's results rather than
\ opening a second one.
Details A blank field in FindCriteria is not a filter: Text blank matches
\ every payee and memo, a blank date bound is open-ended, a blank
\ Amount matches every amount, and a blank Account matches every
\ account.
\
\ Amount is exact unless a range is asked for. It used to be a pair of
\ bounds and nothing else, and a pair of bounds with the upper one left
\ blank matches everything above the number typed -- which is how a
\ find for 69.38 on the author's own book answered with hundreds of
\ rows, not one of them for 69.38. A person who remembers an amount
\ remembers the amount, not an interval around it, so exact is what the
\ dialog opens on and what one field means.
\
\ A range is still worth having, because somewhere between four and
\ five hundred is a real thing to remember. So AmountMatch chooses
\ between the two, and the second field is there only when Range is
\ chosen -- see the second amount field is only there for a range. A
\ range includes both of its ends, and a blank end is open-ended: the
\ behaviour that was a trap while it was the only behaviour is a fair
\ answer once somebody has said the word Range.
\
\ Amount is compared on the absolute value, so 89.99 finds both a
\ payment of -89.99 and a deposit of 89.99: whoever is looking rarely
\ remembers which column it was in. A range compares that same
\ absolute value against its ends, so 40.00 to 100.00 finds the
\ payment of -89.99 as readily as a deposit of it. It is also compared against each
\ line of a split, because the amount that is remembered is as often
\ the one on the receipt as the total the register shows. A split
\ matched by one of its lines is still one result -- the transaction as
\ the register reads it, with --Split-- for its category -- because the
\ line is not a thing a register can be scrolled to.
\
\ Account matches a category the same way a real account's, and
\ matches a transaction if either side of it is the named account or
\ anything beneath it.
\
\ FindResultRow names the transaction the way a register names the
\ other side of a transfer: Account is the side the result is read
\ under, and Category is the other side of it. Scoped to one register,
\ that is always the register searched. Scoped to every register, a
\ transaction that matches on both sides of a transfer is a row under
\ each, because there is no one register it belongs to more than the
\ other.

DataType FindScope
Description Which registers a find looks through.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value          | Notes                                    |
| CurrentRegister | Only the register open in the active tab |
| AllRegisters   | Every account in the book                 |

DataType AmountMatch
Description Whether the amount typed is the amount wanted or one end of an
\ interval it falls in.
Examples: EnumerationValues
| Value | Notes                                               |
| Exact | One field, and the amount matches it                |
| Range | Two fields, and the amount falls between them        |

Attributes FindCriteria
| Attribute   | Type        | Default         |
| Text        | Text        | none            |
| DateFrom    | Text        | none            |
| DateTo      | Text        | none            |
| AmountMatch | AmountMatch | Exact           |
| Amount      | Money       | none            |
| AmountTo    | Money       | none            |
| Account     | AccountPath | none            |
| Scope       | FindScope   | CurrentRegister |

Attributes AmountFieldsShown
| Attribute   | Type        | Default |
| Match       | AmountMatch | Exact   |
| FieldsShown | Integer     | 1       |
| FirstLabel  | Text        | Amount  |
| SecondLabel | Text        | none    |

Attributes FindResultRow
| Attribute | Type           | Default    |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |            |
| Date      | Date           | 2024-01-01 |
| Payee     | PayeeName      | none       |
| Account   | AccountPath    |            |
| Category  | Text           | none       |
| Amount    | Money          | 0.00       |

