BusinessRule The second amount field is only there for a range
Description The dropdown is beside the amount, and it says Exact or Range.
\ On Exact there is one field, labelled Amount. On Range there are
\ two, and the first one's label changes to say which end it is.
Details A rule rather than a scenario, because whether a field is on the
\ screen is not something the model holds -- FindCriteria is what was
\ asked for, not what the dialog looked like when it was asked.
\
\ A dropdown rather than two fields that are always there. Two fields
\ always visible is what the dialog had, and the reason it misbehaved
\ was that nothing on the screen said what leaving one of them blank
\ would do. Choosing Range is the sentence that says it.
\
\ Switching back to Exact hides the second field and clears it, so a
\ number left behind cannot narrow a later find that no longer shows
\ it. Switching to Range leaves the first field alone, since the
\ amount already typed is the sensible lower end.
Examples: AmountFieldsShown
| Match | FieldsShown | FirstLabel   | SecondLabel |
| Exact | 1           | Amount       | none        |
| Range | 2           | Amount~from  | to          |

