Description Choosing a result goes to the transaction in the register the
\ result is read under -- the Account column of the result, not
\ whichever register happens to be open. That is the whole use of
\ the column being there: a find scoped to every register lists
\ matches from accounts the reader is not looking at, and a result
\ under Savings has to open Savings. The results stay open while it
\ happens, because a find is usually a list to work down rather
\ than one line to reach.
Details Going to a result is going to the transaction, so it is the same
\ operation the report's "Go to the transaction..." performs: the
\ register opens and the transaction's line in it is selected. A
\ result names its register, so unlike the report's version nothing
\ has to be chosen -- a transfer matched under both of its sides is
\ two results, and each goes to its own.

Attributes FindResultChoice
Description Which result was chosen, counting from one in the order the
\ results are listed.
| Attribute | Type    | Default |
| Line      | Integer | 1       |

