Description A result has a menu on it, and what is on the menu depends on the
\ transaction the result names. Going to the transaction is there
\ because a menu that cannot do the obvious thing is a surprise, and
\ Show split is there when the transaction is a split -- which is the
\ one thing a result row cannot say for itself. The row reads
\ --Split-- and nothing more, and a find that reached it by one of
\ its lines reached it by a number the row does not show, so the
\ question "which line was that" is the question a split result
\ raises.
Details Show split is left off a transaction that is not a split rather than
\ offered and refused. The account tree greys Delete because an
\ account that cannot be deleted raises a question the reason answers;
\ a transaction with one category raises no question about its split.
\
\ Recategorize will join this menu. It is not here yet because
\ recategorising from a find has to decide what a selection of results
\ from several registers means, and that is a separate piece of work.

