| MatchType | Contains  |
| Payee     | SHELL OIL |
| Category  | none      |
| Enabled   | true      |
# Uncategorized is not a category anybody chose, so it is not offered as one. A
# rule carrying it would put every future visit back in the bucket it is the
# program's job to empty.

Description The category on a rule is chosen from the list of categories, the
\ same way the register's Recategorize chooses one, rather than typed
\ into a box.
Details Typed, a category was a string nobody checked. A rule carrying
\ Expenses:Grocerys matched every visit to the shop and then wrote a
\ category that does not exist, so the rule looked right in the list
\ of rules and the transactions went on arriving in Uncategorized.
\ Nothing said so, because nothing had any reason to look.
\
\ So the field is a button onto the category picker, and what comes
\ back from it is a path that is in the book. The matching rule is the
\ one in the finding-a-category section of Accounts: any segment of a
\ path, an alias standing for exactly one, the unused left out. There
\ is one picker in the program and this is it, reached from a second
\ place.
\
\ Left empty is still how a rule says it tidies the name and leaves
\ the category alone, so the picker can be cancelled and the field
\ stays as it was.

