Description The menu on a selection applies the payee rules to the lines
\ selected, which is the whole-book pass narrowed to what is in front
\ of somebody.
Details Applying the rules to the whole book is the right thing after a long
\ import and the wrong thing while working through one statement.
\ Twenty lines of a register are what a person is actually looking at,
\ and a rule written one minute ago is meant for those twenty -- not
\ for twenty years, where it will also rewrite transactions that were
\ already right and that nobody asked about.
\
\ So it is the same pass over the same rules, in the same order, with
\ the same counts reported; only the set of transactions it is given
\ is different. See how a rule is applied in Payees, which this does
\ not change.

Scenario Applying the payee rules to a selection changes only what is selected
