# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reconciling an account against what the bank said
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description Reconciling is the question the register's two balances raise,
\ answered in one place.
Details The top of every register says what the book has cleared and what the
\ last download said, and the difference between them. Where that
\ difference is not zero, something is in flight or something is
\ wrong, and the way to find out which is to go through what is not
\ cleared yet and tick off what the statement shows. That is
\ reconciling, and it is reached from the account's own menu because
\ it is done to an account rather than to a selection.
\
\ The window shows the two figures, the difference, and every line of
\ the account that is not cleared. Ticking a line clears it and the
\ figures move as it is ticked -- the difference closing to zero is
\ the whole of the work, and watching it close is how somebody knows
\ which tick was the one that mattered.
\
\ What is left when there is nothing more to tick is the part nobody
\ can explain. That is offered as a Balance Adjustment: one
\ transaction for the difference, dated the day the balance was
\ stated, which makes the book agree with the bank. It is written
\ uncleared, so the register still shows the difference and the
\ adjustment is the line that says what it was. Clearing it is a
\ deliberate act and means the figure is accepted; most of the time
\ it is left alone, as a standing note of something never found.

Attributes Reconciliation
Description The reconciling window. Cleared is the book's cleared balance in the
\ display sign of the account; OnLine is what the last download said,
\ with never standing in for an account no download has reached.
\ Difference is Cleared less OnLine, and Agrees is whether there is a
\ stated balance and the difference is nothing.
| Attribute  | Type        | Default |
| Shown      | Boolean     | false   |
| Account    | AccountPath | none    |
| Balance    | Money       | 0.00    |
| Cleared    | Money       | 0.00    |
| OnLine     | Money       | 0.00    |
| OnLineAt   | Text        | never   |
| Difference | Money       | 0.00    |
| Agrees     | Boolean     | false   |

Attributes UnclearedItem
Description One line of the account that is not cleared, offered to be ticked.
\ The amount is signed the way the register shows it -- a payment is
\ negative -- because a statement is read by its figures and the sign
\ is what tells a payment from a deposit.
| Attribute | Type           | Default    |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |            |
| Date      | Date           | 2024-01-01 |
| Payee     | PayeeName      | none       |
| Amount    | Money          | 0.00       |

Attributes ClearedTick
Description A line ticked in the reconciling window, named by its ref.
| Attribute | Type           | Default |
| Ref       | TransactionRef |         |

Attributes BalanceAdjustmentOffer
Description What the window offers to write for a difference nobody could
\ explain. Shown false is the ordinary end of reconciling -- the
\ figures agree and there is nothing to adjust.
| Attribute | Type          | Default    |
| Shown     | Boolean       | false      |
| Amount    | Money         | 0.00       |
| Date      | Date          | 2024-01-01 |
| Payee     | PayeeName     | none       |
| Category  | AccountPath   | none       |
| Cleared   | ClearedStatus | Uncleared  |

Scenario Reconciling shows the two balances and what is not cleared yet
